For the maintainer, the two candidates:

  Apache License 2.0   https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt
                       permissive, with an explicit patent grant and a NOTICE convention; common for
                       infrastructure and tooling that companies adopt.

  MIT License          https://opensource.org/license/mit
                       permissive and as short as a license gets; the most common choice for small tools.

Either fits this project. Apache-2.0 is the safer default if you expect companies to use it; MIT if you want the
least friction. To choose, replace this file with the license's full text, put the year and your name in its
copyright line, and set `license` in pyproject.toml to match.

Third-party notes: cloud/nvenc-gpu-filter.c names a few constants and structure layouts of NVIDIA's driver interface,
as published in NVIDIA's open-gpu-kernel-modules (MIT/GPL-2.0 dual license); no code is copied from it. The tests and
the example use Playwright (Apache-2.0), numpy (BSD-3-Clause) and ffmpeg (LGPL/GPL, run as a separate program, not
bundled).
